aqrw|n|An involuntary act, excited by drowsiness, etc., consisting of a deep and long inspiration following several successive attempts at inspiration, the mouth, fauces, etc., being wide open. ; The act of opening wide, or of gaping. ; A chasm, mouth, or passageway.	a:aqrw,118,1;5t0v,93,4;8a3v,68,5;2o4c,59,3;wyo,47,12;96ey,30,2~wyo,47,12;8a3v,68,5;5t0v,93,4;2o4c,59,3;96ey,30,2;aqrw,118,1	v:96ey,20,1;a6ev,6,4~a6ev,6,4;96ey,20,1	n:aqrw,153,12;5t0v,89,3;wyo,11,1~aqrw,153,12;5t0v,89,3;wyo,11,1	N:aqrw,153,12;a8we,15,4~aqrw,153,12;a8we,15,4
aqrw|v|To open the mouth involuntarily through drowsiness, dullness, or fatigue; to gape; to oscitate. ; To open wide; to gape, as if to allow the entrance or exit of anything. ; To open the mouth, or to gape, through surprise or bewilderment. ; To be eager; to desire to swallow anything; to express desire by yawning; as, to yawn for fat livings.	s:70j5,27,8~70j5,27,8
